WEBVTT

00:28.020 --> 00:29.180
It's you...

00:29.190 --> 00:30.730
You're the one who's evil.

00:30.730 --> 00:31.730
If only you weren't here...

00:34.320 --> 00:36.190
You... you...

00:59.520 --> 01:08.300
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:08.330 --> 01:17.330
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:17.380 --> 01:24.140
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:26.720 --> 01:32.820
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:34.960 --> 01:43.560
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:43.600 --> 01:50.200
And I'm faced with another day

01:51.410 --> 01:57.210
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:57.250 --> 02:01.740
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

02:01.790 --> 02:05.880
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:05.920 --> 02:10.450
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

02:10.500 --> 02:14.930
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:14.970 --> 02:22.770
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:28.060 --> 02:28.150
AZUKI ARAI

02:28.060 --> 02:28.150
Bean Washer

03:01.140 --> 03:03.600
This isn't going to do me any good...

03:11.480 --> 03:12.690
It'll get wet!

03:17.280 --> 03:21.410
Jeez... It's getting all hazy.

03:25.790 --> 03:26.660
All right!

03:52.690 --> 03:55.980
[Note: A Japanese ghost that stalks people as they walk at
night, said to disappear if you recite a specific charm.]

03:52.690 --> 03:55.480
You're a Betobeto-san, right?

03:55.690 --> 03:58.490
Then I just need to recite the charm...

03:59.700 --> 04:03.240
Betobeto-san, Betobeto-san, go ahead... erm... around...

04:03.990 --> 04:05.410
All right, that should have...

04:10.540 --> 04:12.460
I can't stop!

04:13.750 --> 04:15.170
A cliff?

04:41.030 --> 04:44.120
I don't know who you are, but...

04:46.370 --> 04:47.790
Are you all right?

04:48.950 --> 04:53.790
This is not a place for someone like you.

04:55.040 --> 04:56.880
Why don't you go back?

04:57.340 --> 05:00.010
There is a mountain hut where you can stay If you do.

05:23.820 --> 05:26.070
I can't climb this, that's for sure...

05:35.210 --> 05:38.130
A store in a place like this?

05:58.570 --> 05:59.650
Excuse me, sir.

06:01.610 --> 06:03.070
Do you live here?

06:04.700 --> 06:07.530
No, I'm just lost...

06:07.530 --> 06:09.530
Then, we must be in a similar situation.

06:10.580 --> 06:13.080
There aren't any other houses nearby.

06:13.370 --> 06:16.540
I guess we'll have to seek shelter from the rain here.

06:17.590 --> 06:20.840
Do you suppose anyone still lives here?

06:26.090 --> 06:27.720
That was close!

06:28.680 --> 06:29.550
A sign?

06:30.430 --> 06:31.760
Bichuuya?

06:36.060 --> 06:37.600
Who might you be?

06:38.110 --> 06:43.070
Sorry to impose on you, but because of the sudden rain...

06:43.070 --> 06:45.190
Oh, please come in...

06:45.950 --> 06:46.900
Thank you.

06:56.710 --> 06:59.200
I'm sorry about all the dust.

06:59.360 --> 07:01.360
Please, don't worry about it.

07:02.330 --> 07:06.330
In its time, this place was quite busy.

07:06.880 --> 07:09.050
Do you live alone here, sir?

07:09.310 --> 07:09.980
Yes.

07:10.300 --> 07:12.760
By the way, my name is Tokuemon.

07:18.310 --> 07:19.520
That sound...?

07:19.770 --> 07:22.070
Is something wrong?

07:22.150 --> 07:22.570
N-No...

07:26.920 --> 07:27.840
Umm...

07:28.120 --> 07:28.750
Yes?

07:28.840 --> 07:30.780
I think the rain has given me the chills...

07:30.960 --> 07:34.190
May I use your bathroom?

07:34.410 --> 07:37.420
Down the hall and to your right.

07:37.470 --> 07:38.500
Thank you!

07:42.750 --> 07:45.460
Have we met somewhere before?

07:46.270 --> 07:47.020
No...

07:52.650 --> 07:56.320
Huh? Which way did I come from?

07:57.990 --> 07:59.320
I'm saved.

08:02.490 --> 08:03.620
Excuse me!

08:14.710 --> 08:15.840
Kid!

08:16.380 --> 08:17.750
Hey, kid!

08:19.300 --> 08:21.630
What are you looking at?

08:22.260 --> 08:24.970
Hurry up and close the screen.

08:25.050 --> 08:27.140
S-Sorry!

08:27.140 --> 08:29.100
I-I didn't mean to...

08:29.230 --> 08:31.390
I came to the wrong room and...

08:31.390 --> 08:32.480
Whatever, just close the screen.

08:33.190 --> 08:34.310
S-Sorry!!!

08:39.490 --> 08:41.150
Is something wrong?

08:41.990 --> 08:46.160
No, except... you told you were alone,
but there's also a woman...

08:46.160 --> 08:50.120
Oh... She's seeking refuge from the rain just as you are.

08:50.200 --> 08:51.620
Oh, I see.

08:55.330 --> 08:58.960
You? Thank you for saving me earlier...

08:59.800 --> 09:03.510
Apparently, you do not listen when
other people give you advice.

09:04.390 --> 09:05.180
What?

09:05.430 --> 09:11.220
After all the trouble I went through to try and spare
you from having a frightful experience, too...

09:11.480 --> 09:13.180
What does that mean?

09:15.730 --> 09:18.270
Per-ve-rt.

09:18.690 --> 09:21.570
H-Hey! It was just a misunderstanding!

09:26.280 --> 09:27.870
Th-This sound, it's...!

09:28.200 --> 09:29.330
Sound?

09:29.490 --> 09:31.830
The sound of the rain is annoying, isn't it?

09:32.000 --> 09:35.620
Can't you hear it? That sound... going "rasp, rasp"?

09:35.620 --> 09:37.710
Are you sure you're not just imagining things?

09:37.710 --> 09:40.380
No, I can hear it.

09:40.460 --> 09:42.880
Yeah... this sound...

09:43.420 --> 09:45.800
[Note: Azuki are a type of red bean.]

09:43.420 --> 09:45.800
It sounds like somebody is washing azuki, doesn't it?

09:46.050 --> 09:47.340
Azuki...

09:47.640 --> 09:50.220
[Note: Azuki Arai literally translates to "Red Bean Washer".]

09:47.640 --> 09:50.220
I wonder if we'll see an Azuki Arai...

09:50.850 --> 09:53.770
An Azuki Arai? What's that?

09:54.440 --> 09:58.020
[Note: Mononoke is normally translated as 'spirit', but
refers to supernatural entitles in general.]

09:54.440 --> 09:58.020
An Azuki Arai is a type of mononoke.

09:58.360 --> 10:02.530
It's said that it makes a noise that sounds like they're
washing azuki near rivers or underneath bridges.

10:02.570 --> 10:06.280
For some reason, you can't see them.

10:06.950 --> 10:08.950
A mononoke?

10:09.370 --> 10:11.490
That's just superstition.

10:11.490 --> 10:12.870
Superstition?

10:13.410 --> 10:15.910
[Note: Fuda are pieces of paper that are inscribed with charms.]

10:13.410 --> 10:15.910
But you make your living selling fuda, don't you?

10:16.170 --> 10:21.340
In other words, you take advantage of belief in curses
and mononoke to put food on your table.

10:21.420 --> 10:24.590
While I am inclined to applaud you for your theory,

10:25.090 --> 10:27.760
my profession as a fuda seller is merely for sustenance.

10:27.970 --> 10:31.350
I believe in neither gods nor buddhas.

10:32.930 --> 10:34.930
I knew it. It's an Azuki Arai.

10:35.430 --> 10:39.230
It's said that if you hear this sound, then
you're going to fall in the water.

10:39.360 --> 10:44.320
Mister, you're more than just a pervert... you have
knowledge of all sorts of strange things.

10:44.490 --> 10:46.440
Th-The pervert part was uncalled for!

10:46.950 --> 10:51.490
Even though I may not look the part, I make my living using
my head by thinking up riddles for children and such.

10:51.620 --> 10:56.330
[Note: Kaidan are tales of supernatural occurrences in everyday life.]

10:51.620 --> 10:56.330
In the future, I want to publish a book
of 100 kaidan that I've collected.

10:57.210 --> 11:00.200
[Note: It is believed that if you tell 100 supernatural tales you
will experience the supernatural after the 100th.]

10:57.210 --> 10:59.460
You're collecting 100 stories?

10:59.500 --> 11:02.290
I love scary stories.

11:02.750 --> 11:03.610
I see...

11:04.050 --> 11:07.670
Masters of the written arts are indeed knowledgeable.

11:07.680 --> 11:08.970
That's...

11:09.180 --> 11:10.930
I'm still just a novice.

11:12.140 --> 11:15.520
There is indeed an Azuki Arai.

11:18.270 --> 11:24.020
It is the reason that this place, Bichuuya,
has come to such ruin.

11:26.610 --> 11:30.070
Yes... that was ten years ago.

11:32.320 --> 11:37.040
Back when this shop was still prosperous,
an apprentice called Yasuke came.

11:37.250 --> 11:43.040
He couldn't do any work, but he
had one very strange talent.

11:43.420 --> 11:48.470
He could tell the number of azuki
in a box just by looking at it.

11:49.010 --> 11:51.680
Rumors of his ability spread from town to town,

11:51.680 --> 11:57.180
until even the lord of this land said that
he wished to see Yasuke's ability.

11:58.180 --> 12:02.850
Yasuke perfectly guessed the number of azuki.

12:03.810 --> 12:09.320
This pleased the lord and the story came to
be known throughout the whole country,

12:06.760 --> 12:09.740
Bichuuya

12:09.320 --> 12:12.820
bringing unforeseen prosperity to this store.

12:13.370 --> 12:14.910
However...

12:15.080 --> 12:21.160
I, who was greatly pleased by all this, said
that I would turn over my fortune to him.

12:21.370 --> 12:23.460
In front of all the employees, too.

12:24.170 --> 12:31.130
I had no children of my own and was
possibly over-infatuated with him.

12:33.470 --> 12:39.560
The next day Yasuke went to
wash azuki and then vanished.

12:42.230 --> 12:44.350
It was a sad end...

12:48.230 --> 12:55.240
After that incident, on rainy days like
this, people heard a strange sound.

12:55.870 --> 12:57.780
That was the Azuki Arai.

12:57.790 --> 13:03.370
A rumor started that Yasuke's emotions,
with nowhere to go, had become a ghost.

13:03.370 --> 13:08.630
One by one, the shop's employees left until
the shop came to its current state.

13:11.510 --> 13:13.630
That must have been very hard.

13:14.010 --> 13:17.100
Did you find the murderer?

13:17.470 --> 13:24.770
Indeed, it was my clerk of many
years, a man named Tatsugorou.

13:25.690 --> 13:28.110
He was a very serious person.

13:28.570 --> 13:31.440
He was executed.

13:31.440 --> 13:32.400
Executed?

13:33.070 --> 13:34.700
What's wrong?

13:34.780 --> 13:37.160
You look pale.

13:37.950 --> 13:39.120
Somebody's there!

13:47.380 --> 13:50.260
There shouldn't be anyone.

14:00.940 --> 14:03.150
Don't scare me like that.

14:05.320 --> 14:08.030
It's quite late now.

14:08.200 --> 14:11.780
It must be fate that I've brought up
such an old tale with all of you.

14:11.780 --> 14:13.120
Please, stay here tonight.

14:14.620 --> 14:19.130
You know, there's really nothing surprising
about Yasuke coming back as a ghost.

14:19.420 --> 14:22.790
He was killed even though he had done nothing wrong.

14:22.790 --> 14:23.790
Yeah.

14:23.800 --> 14:26.210
Well, if he does appear,

14:26.210 --> 14:30.380
we've got a great priest named Enkai to drive him away.

14:30.930 --> 14:33.010
How did he know my name?

14:33.720 --> 14:37.310
Even so, this has become a really weird case...

14:38.060 --> 14:39.810
The rain just won't stop...

14:40.730 --> 14:41.730
No,

14:42.480 --> 14:44.520
this isn't Bichuuya.

14:45.070 --> 14:47.820
Bichuuya shouldn't be out here in the country.

14:47.820 --> 14:48.740
And...

14:49.360 --> 14:52.030
And Tokuemon-san should already be dead.

14:55.740 --> 14:58.120
I can't complain, I guess...

15:27.360 --> 15:28.360
A-azuki!

15:39.950 --> 15:41.710
What's wrong?

15:43.120 --> 15:45.580
Did you have a bad dream or something?

15:45.840 --> 15:46.750
Y-Yes...

15:55.050 --> 15:57.760
Go awayl Go awayl

15:59.560 --> 16:02.430
What's wrong? Tatsugorou-niichan...

16:03.520 --> 16:06.150
No, I'm not Tatsugorou!

16:06.520 --> 16:06.810
I'm not!

16:06.860 --> 16:08.980
I'm not!!!

16:10.490 --> 16:11.900
Ouch!

16:12.110 --> 16:13.570
What the hell was that for?

16:45.650 --> 16:46.770
Th-This place is...

16:50.530 --> 16:53.650
Somebody! Somebody has to be there?! Open up!

16:53.650 --> 16:55.700
Please, open the door!

16:59.550 --> 17:00.380
I...

17:01.790 --> 17:02.870
I'm not evil!

17:03.530 --> 17:04.450
I...

17:05.040 --> 17:07.330
I worked honestly.

17:07.710 --> 17:12.380
If the master hadn't said that he'd give
the property to that... that little kid...

17:13.050 --> 17:14.550
If he hadn't said that...

18:00.140 --> 18:02.220
Tatsugorou-niichan...?

18:08.520 --> 18:09.520
Huh?

18:12.400 --> 18:14.360
Yasuke!

18:31.420 --> 18:32.650
Enkai-san!

18:38.720 --> 18:40.930
Mataichi... san?

18:51.600 --> 18:55.070
I... I served in my apprenticeship honestly...

18:55.440 --> 18:58.530
For ages... always, always...

18:59.610 --> 19:00.740
All the same...

19:00.860 --> 19:04.160
all the same, the master turned over
his precious wealth to Yasuke.

19:04.160 --> 19:05.620
To a kid like that...

19:07.370 --> 19:08.370
That's why...

19:09.000 --> 19:11.000
That's why, I...!

19:12.130 --> 19:14.750
That is the way of this world.

19:16.840 --> 19:22.090
The unworthy amass great wealth
and the honest man falls to ruin.

19:22.800 --> 19:25.720
This world is filled with such mysteries.

19:26.390 --> 19:30.810
What is right and what is wrong, none can tell.

19:31.480 --> 19:34.190
However, to murder another person...

19:34.400 --> 19:36.230
That is truly a crime!

19:55.920 --> 19:57.250
This is...

20:04.720 --> 20:05.930
What the hell?

20:23.110 --> 20:24.820
He looks pitiful.

20:24.910 --> 20:27.780
Perhaps you overdid it.

20:28.450 --> 20:31.700
Isn't that always how it is? Him overdoing it, I mean.

20:32.120 --> 20:35.750
But doesn't he look peaceful?

20:39.880 --> 20:42.630
The deed has been done.

20:48.760 --> 20:49.510
There you are!

20:51.560 --> 20:53.520
I found you guys!

20:54.110 --> 20:56.060
Who are you?

20:56.730 --> 20:58.110
Who, me?

20:58.110 --> 20:59.900
A paltry seller of fuda, that's all.

21:00.020 --> 21:01.570
So you say,

21:01.650 --> 21:06.570
[Note: A komataguri is a man who makes his living deceiving other with words.]

21:01.650 --> 21:06.570
but in reality you're a komatakuguri who makes
his living deceiving others, aren't you Mataichi?

21:06.780 --> 21:10.450
A yamanekomawashi is a puppeteer

21:06.780 --> 21:10.450
What about you, Ogin? You yamanekomawashi!

21:10.540 --> 21:12.490
My, how untactful of you.

21:12.500 --> 21:14.370
There they go again...

21:19.920 --> 21:21.880
Aren't you just murderers?

21:30.010 --> 21:34.220
Now do you understand, Mr. Pervert Writer?

21:34.730 --> 21:37.640
Don't get too close too us for your own good...

21:38.440 --> 21:42.360
If you don't listen to people's warnings, then you'll get hurt.

21:52.330 --> 21:55.700
Just who were those people?

22:01.710 --> 22:06.120
That was my first encounter with Mataichi and his gang...

22:06.180 --> 22:11.710
and the world of darkness that was with them.

22:15.160 --> 22:20.690
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:22.630 --> 22:28.730
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:29.710 --> 22:35.470
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:35.510 --> 22:42.110
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:43.520 --> 22:49.460
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:49.490 --> 22:56.160
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:57.000 --> 23:06.470
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.780 --> 23:10.970
Draw near

23:11.250 --> 23:18.240
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:18.290 --> 23:24.230
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:26.400 --> 23:31.660
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:31.700 --> 23:40.110
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:49.010 --> 23:51.090
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness,

23:51.090 --> 23:54.140
leaving only a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:55.310 --> 24:00.350
[Note: Yanagi means willow.]

23:55.310 --> 23:57.520
A yanagi continues to protect Yanagiya,

23:57.520 --> 24:00.350
a well-established inn in the happy city of Edo.

24:01.060 --> 24:03.230
Out of sheer love for its master, Kichibee,

24:03.480 --> 24:06.190
it kills the bride who married into the household.

24:06.610 --> 24:10.740
Next time on Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:11.160 --> 24:12.370
Yanagi Onna

24:12.950 --> 24:15.660
The deed has been done.
